.TH DFTE\-GTK 1 2026-10-30 "dfte-gtk 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dfte\-gtk \- desktop app for sending files directly to a nearby device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dfte\-gtk
.RB [ \-\-page
.IR page ]
.RI [ file ...]
.br
.B dfte\-gtk
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.br
.B dfte\-gtk
.BR \-V | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dfte\-gtk
is the GTK 4 and libadwaita front end of DFTE for Linux desktops.
It sends files and folders straight to another device on the same network, or
to an Android phone over Wi\-Fi Direct, with no server, account or Internet
connection.
The other device can run
.BR dfte\-gtk ,
.BR dfte (1)
or the DFTE Android app.
.PP
While the window is open the computer is ready to receive: it listens on port
47821 (any free port if that one is taken) and announces itself on the local
network.
Incoming transfers are offered in a dialog first.
.PP
The window has five pages:
.TP
.B Send
Pick files or a folder, or drop them anywhere on the window, then choose a
device found nearby or type an address such as 192.168.1.20:47821.
.TP
.B Receive
This computer's name and the addresses it listens on.
The Wi\-Fi Direct box connects to a phone by its Wi\-Fi Direct name; see
.BR NOTES .
.TP
.B Activity
Running and finished transfers.
.TP
.B Devices
Trusted devices.
Removing one makes the next connection ask for the code again.
.TP
.B Settings
Device name, fingerprint and the Downloads folder.
.PP
The first time two devices connect, a dialog shows the other device's name,
fingerprint and a six\-digit code.
Choose
.B Codes match
only if the other device shows the same six digits.
Tick
.B Trust this device
to skip the comparison next time.
There is no way to skip it on a first connection.
.PP
Only one instance runs per user session (application id
.BR dev.dfte.Dfte ).
Starting the program again brings the existing window forward; files and
.B \-\-page
given to that second launch are ignored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " page"
Open on this page:
.BR send ,
.BR receive ,
.BR activity ,
.B devices
or
.BR settings .
The default is
.BR send .
.TP
.IR file ...
Files or folders to send.
They are preselected on the Send page, which suits an "Open with" entry in a
file manager.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit without opening a window.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
Other options starting with
.B \-\-
are ignored.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DFTE_DEVICE_NAME
Name shown to other devices.
Default: the host name.
.TP
.B DFTE_LOG
Log filter in
.B tracing\-subscriber
syntax, for example
.B info
or
.BR dfte_core=debug .
Default:
.BR warn .
Logs go to standard error and never contain keys or file contents.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base for the state directory, see
.BR FILES .
Default:
.IR ~/.local/share .
.TP
.B XDG_DOWNLOAD_DIR
Where received files go.
If unset, it is read from
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/user\-dirs.dirs ,
falling back to
.IR ~/Downloads .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where
.I user\-dirs.dirs
is looked up.
Default:
.IR ~/.config .
.PP
The app follows the system's light or dark setting.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/dfte/
State directory, shared with
.BR dfte (1):
.I identity.key
(the device's secret key, mode 0600),
.I trusted.json
(trusted devices) and
.I staging/
(partial downloads and resume state).
The two programs are the same device to everyone else.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/dfte/hashes/
Sender's cache of file hashes, shared with
.BR dfte (1).
Safe to delete.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the window is closed normally.
1 when the engine could not start; the reason is shown in a dialog and
logged to standard error.
In that case (for example, an unreadable identity key) the app shows the
reason in a dialog and quits when it is dismissed, so check the dialog rather
than the exit status.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open on the Receive page:
.PP
.RS
.EX
dfte\-gtk \-\-page receive
.EE
.RE
.PP
Start with two items ready to send:
.PP
.RS
.EX
dfte\-gtk ~/Videos/holiday.mp4 ~/Pictures/trip
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run with debug logging from the engine:
.PP
.RS
.EX
DFTE_LOG=dfte_core=debug dfte\-gtk
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
Wi\-Fi Direct goes through NetworkManager and needs no root.
The phone must have DFTE open on its Send or Receive screen, and on Android 12
or older its Location switch must be on.
If this computer ends up owning the group, NetworkManager needs
.B dnsmasq
installed to give the phone an address.
.PP
There is no desktop entry or package yet; run the binary from the build
directory or copy it somewhere on your
.BR PATH .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dfte (1),
.BR nmcli (1)
.PP
The project's
.I docs/wifi\-direct.md
and
.IR docs/security.md .
